---
description: AI Rules Location
globs: *.mdc
---
# AI Rules Location

Rules for placing and organizing AI rule files in the repository.

<rule>
name: ai_rules_location
description: Standards for placing AI rule files in the correct directory
filters:
  # Match any .mdc files
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.mdc$"
  # Match files that look like AI rules
  - type: content
    pattern: "(?s)<rule>.*?</rule>"
  # Match file creation events
  - type: event
    pattern: "file_create"

actions:
  - type: reject
    conditions:
      - pattern: "^(?!\\/ai-rules\\/.*\\.mdc$)"
        message: "AI rule files (.mdc) must be placed in the /ai-rules directory"

  - type: suggest
    message: |
      When creating AI rules:

      1. Always place rule files in PROJECT_ROOT/ai-rules/:
         ```
         /ai-rules/
         ├── your-rule-name.mdc
         ├── another-rule.mdc
         └── ...
         ```

      2. Follow the naming convention:
         - Use kebab-case for filenames
         - Always use .mdc extension
         - Make names descriptive of the rule's purpose

      3. Directory structure:
         ```
         PROJECT_ROOT/
         ├── ai-rules/
         │       ├── your-rule-name.mdc
         │       └── ...
         └── ...
         ```

      4. Never place rule files:
         - In the project root
         - In subdirectories outside /ai-rules
         - In any other location

examples:
  - input: |
      # Bad: Rule file in wrong location
      rules/my-rule.mdc
      my-rule.mdc
      .rules/my-rule.mdc

      # Good: Rule file in correct location
      /ai-rules/my-rule.mdc
    output: "Correctly placed AI rule file"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
</rule>